  "title": "Global Tech: Optical Networking - The next mega trend in AI infrastructure",
  "type": "sector",
  "priority": "medium",
  "published": "2026-08-11",
  "insights": [
   "Networking is the next frontier in AI infrastructure, with a projected 9x TAM expansion to US$154bn by 2028 driven by AI server ramp-ups and specification upgrades.",
   "Dollar content per computing unit is expected to increase 16x for scale-out and 45x for scale-up configurations as the industry migrates from GB300 NVL72 to Rubin Ultra NVL576.",
   "Co-packaged optics (CPO) is a critical growth driver, projected to contribute US$91bn (59%) of the total US$154bn TAM, assuming a 29% penetration rate in scale-out connections.",
   "Pluggable optical modules will continue to see growth in dollar content per rack despite CPO adoption, with 1.6T equivalent units increasing from 216 in GB300 to 2.5k in Rubin Ultra.",
   "Supply chain tightness for EML and CW lasers is expected to persist through 2027, with potential balancing in 2H28 due to capacity expansions and a shift toward inferencing.",
   "Silicon photonics (SiPh) penetration in the datacom market is forecast to grow from 6% in 1Q24 to 46% by 4Q28, driven by integration, power efficiency, and cost advantages.",
   "Optical Circuit Switches (OCS) are emerging as an optimal solution for fast-changing AI clusters, allowing for bandwidth upgrades without replacing the switch infrastructure.",
